      en: "Prasat Kravan Temple is located in Siem Reap Province, about 20 km south of Angkor Wat. Built in 921 AD under King Harshavarman I, it consists of five brick towers on a common platform. The temple is dedicated to the Hindu god Vishnu. Inner walls feature bas-reliefs of Vishnu and Lakshmi. The temple was restored by the French in the 1930s. The name 'Prasat Kravan' means 'Cardamom Temple'.",
