      en: "The Lolei Terrace is an elevated platform at the Lolei temple complex in Roluos, built in the late 9th century under King Yasovarman I. It served as a base for the temple towers and as a ceremonial area. Made of laterite and sandstone with decorative friezes, it offers views of the surrounding landscape. It is part of the early Angkorian urban center Hariharalaya.",
